From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:55:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ims: give the compat ImsService adapters a default executor

Binding any compat ImsService (android.telephony.ims.compat.ImsService --
the path a bridge to an OEM's pre-P com.android.ims stack has to use) kills
com.android.phone immediately and it restart-loops:

  FATAL EXCEPTION: ImsProvisioningController
  java.lang.NullPointerException
    at java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.screenExecutor
    at ImsConfigImplBase$ImsConfigStub.executeMethodAsync
    at ImsConfigImplBase$ImsConfigStub.addImsConfigCallback
    at com.android.ims.ImsConfig.addConfigCallback
    at ImsProvisioningController$MmTelFeatureListener.connectionReady

Every *ImplBase dispatches its binder calls through
CompletableFuture.runAsync(.., executor).join(), and the compat adapters are
constructed without one. A null executor there is not a fall back to the
calling thread -- screenExecutor() throws -- so the first framework call into
an adapter is fatal. ImsService does the equivalent for the modern path in
getConfig/getRegistration/createMmTelFeature; createMMTelCompat() did it for
none of the three adapters it creates.

Use a direct executor rather than this controller's single-threaded
mExecutor. It is what these adapters were written for (they predate the
executor) and what ImsService itself falls back to when an implementation
does not override getExecutor(). Sharing one thread across the three
adapters would also serialize call setup behind the 2s-per-capability
CountDownLatch waits in changeEnabledCapabilities/queryCapabilityConfiguration
-- long enough for the network to cancel an incoming INVITE.

Found bringing LG's Ims4 up on 24.0; the compat path has been deprecated
since P and nothing in tree exercises it.

---
 .../ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java       | 26 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
index 6b9866968c..61531fb9c0 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ import com.android.ims.internal.IImsMMTelFeature;
 import com.android.ims.internal.IImsServiceController;
 import com.android.internal.annotations.VisibleForTesting;
 
+import java.util.concurrent.Executor;
 import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
 
 /**
@@ -264,8 +265,29 @@ public class ImsServiceControllerCompat extends ImsServiceController {
         ImsRegistrationCompatAdapter regAdapter = new ImsRegistrationCompatAdapter();
         mmTelAdapter.addRegistrationAdapter(regAdapter);
         mRegCompatAdapters.put(slotId, regAdapter);
-        mConfigCompatAdapters.put(slotId, new ImsConfigCompatAdapter(
-                mmTelAdapter.getOldConfigInterface()));
+        ImsConfigCompatAdapter configAdapter = new ImsConfigCompatAdapter(
+                mmTelAdapter.getOldConfigInterface());
+        mConfigCompatAdapters.put(slotId, configAdapter);
+        // Every *ImplBase routes its binder calls through
+        // CompletableFuture.runAsync(.., executor).join(). ImsService does the equivalent of this
+        // in getConfig/getRegistration/createMmTelFeature; nothing does it for the compat adapters,
+        // so their executor is null -- and null there is not a fallback to the calling thread,
+        // screenExecutor() throws NPE. The first framework call in (ImsProvisioningController ->
+        // ImsConfig#addConfigCallback) then kills com.android.phone, which restart-loops for as
+        // long as a compat ImsService is bound.
+        //
+        // Run them directly on the calling binder thread, which is both what these adapters were
+        // written for (they predate the executor) and what ImsService falls back to when an
+        // implementation does not override getExecutor(). Do NOT hand them this controller's
+        // single-threaded mExecutor: changeEnabledCapabilities and queryCapabilityConfiguration
+        // block on a 2s CountDownLatch per capability, and sharing one thread across the three
+        // adapters would queue call setup (createCallSession, getPendingCallSession for an
+        // incoming call) behind up to several of those -- long enough for the network to cancel
+        // an incoming INVITE.
+        final Executor directExecutor = Runnable::run;
+        mmTelAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(directExecutor);
+        regAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(directExecutor);
+        configAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(directExecutor);
         return mmTelAdapter.getBinder();
     }
 
